    "text": "Cyanohydrin formation:<br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/150800_2.JPG\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 89px;\" /><br />This reaction is nucleophilic addition reaction.<br />Step (i): The nucleophilic carbon in the cyanide adds to the electrophilic carbon in the polar carbonyl group, electrons from the <math> <mrow> <mtext>C</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>=</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>O</mtext></mrow> </math> move to the electronegative <math> <mtext>O</mtext> </math> creating an intermediate alkoxide.<br />Step (ii): An <math><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow></mrow></math> reaction protonation of the alkoxide oxygen creates the cyanohydrin product.",
